Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usages  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE.CITIBIKE_TRIPS  
  – "starttime", "stoptime": derive calendar day (2018 only) to join to daily‑level weather.  
  – "start_station_latitude", "start_station_longitude": point used with ST_WITHIN to check if it falls inside ZIP‑code 10019 polygon.  
  – "end_station_latitude", "end_station_longitude": same test for ending point.  
  – "usertype": bucket (Customer / Subscriber) whose weather averages we must compare.  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES  
  – "zip_code": look up ‘10019’.  
  – "state_code": further restrict to ‘NY’.  
  – "zip_code_geom": GEOMETRY polygon used together with ST_WITHIN to test trip points.  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.STATIONS  
  – "name": search for ‘CENTRAL PARK’.  
  – "state": confirm ‘NY’.  
  – "usaf","wban": composite key that appears in GSOD20YY tables; needed to isolate the Central Park weather rows.  

• NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1.NOAA_GSOD.GSOD2018  
  – "stn","wban": match to Central Park codes.  
  – "year","mo","da": compose a date that will line up with trip calendar day.  
  – "temp": daily mean temperature.  
  – "prcp": daily precipitation.  
  – "wdsp": daily mean wind speed.  

Conditions typically used  

• "zip_code" = '10019' AND "state_code" = 'NY'  
• ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(long,lat)), "zip_code_geom")  
• DATE(from_unixtime("starttime"/1e6)) BETWEEN '2018‑01‑01' AND '2018‑12‑31'  
• NOAA station rows where UPPER("name") ILIKE '%CENTRAL%PARK%' AND "state" = 'NY'  


Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows)  

```sql
-- 1. Description: Show the NY ZIP‑code polygon for 10019.
SELECT "zip_code",
       "state_code",
       "area_land_meters",
       "zip_code_geom"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"
WHERE "zip_code" = '10019' AND "state_code" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Sample of 2018 Citi Bike trips and their raw lat/lon, still un‑filtered by ZIP.
SELECT "starttime",
       "start_station_latitude",
       "start_station_longitude",
       "end_station_latitude",
       "end_station_longitude",
       "usertype"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE"."CITIBIKE_TRIPS"
WHERE "starttime" BETWEEN 1514764800000000 AND 1546300799000000   -- microsec epoch for 2018
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Return 20 trips whose start point is inside ZIP 10019 (uses ST_WITHIN).
SELECT t."starttime",
       t."usertype"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE"."CITIBIKE_TRIPS"  t
JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"       z
     ON z."zip_code" = '10019' AND z."state_code" = 'NY'
WHERE ST_WITHIN(
          TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."start_station_longitude", t."start_station_latitude")),
          z."zip_code_geom")
      AND t."starttime" BETWEEN 1514764800000000 AND 1546300799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Same idea but require BOTH start & end points within ZIP 10019.
SELECT t."starttime",
       t."usertype"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE"."CITIBIKE_TRIPS"  t
JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"       z
     ON z."zip_code" = '10019' AND z."state_code" = 'NY'
WHERE ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."start_station_longitude", t."start_station_latitude")), z."zip_code_geom")
  AND ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."end_station_longitude"  , t."end_station_latitude"  )), z."zip_code_geom")
  AND t."starttime" BETWEEN 1514764800000000 AND 1546300799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Check distinct user types present in those ZIP‑10019 2018 round‑trips.
SELECT DISTINCT t."usertype"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE"."CITIBIKE_TRIPS"  t
JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"       z
     ON z."zip_code" = '10019' AND z."state_code" = 'NY'
WHERE ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."start_station_longitude", t."start_station_latitude")), z."zip_code_geom")
  AND ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."end_station_longitude"  , t."end_station_latitude"  )), z."zip_code_geom")
  AND t."starttime" BETWEEN 1514764800000000 AND 1546300799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Locate the Central Park weather station record in NOAA metadata.
SELECT "usaf",
       "wban",
       "name",
       "state",
       "lat",
       "lon"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NOAA_GSOD"."STATIONS"
WHERE UPPER("name") ILIKE '%CENTRAL%PARK%' AND "state" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Preview 2018 GSOD rows for that Central Park station.
SELECT "stn",
       "wban",
       "year",
       "mo",
       "da",
       "temp",
       "prcp",
       "wdsp"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NOAA_GSOD"."GSOD2018"
WHERE "stn"  = '725033'   -- replace with codes returned in query 6
  AND "wban" = '94728'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Join CitiBike trip days (zip 10019 round‑trips) to Central Park weather; show temp by usertype.
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('day', TO_TIMESTAMP(t."starttime"/1000000))         AS "trip_day",
       t."usertype",
       w."temp"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE"."CITIBIKE_TRIPS"  t
JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"       z
     ON z."zip_code" = '10019' AND z."state_code" = 'NY'
JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NOAA_GSOD"."GSOD2018"                w
     ON w."stn" = '725033' AND w."wban" = '94728'
     AND w."year" = '2018'
     AND TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP(t."starttime"/1000000)) = TO_DATE(TO_DATE(w."year"||'-'||w."mo"||'-'||w."da'))
WHERE ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."start_station_longitude", t."start_station_latitude")), z."zip_code_geom")
  AND ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."end_station_longitude"  , t."end_station_latitude"  )), z."zip_code_geom")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Aggregate weather variables by user type for those trips.
SELECT t."usertype",
       AVG(w."temp") AS "avg_temp",
       AVG(w."prcp") AS "avg_prcp",
       AVG(w."wdsp") AS "avg_wdsp"
FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE"."CITIBIKE_TRIPS"  t
JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"       z
     ON z."zip_code" = '10019' AND z."state_code" = 'NY'
JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NOAA_GSOD"."GSOD2018"                w
     ON w."stn" = '725033' AND w."wban" = '94728'
     AND w."year" = '2018'
     AND TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP(t."starttime"/1000000)) = TO_DATE(TO_DATE(w."year"||'-'||w."mo"||'-'||w."da'))
WHERE ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."start_station_longitude", t."start_station_latitude")), z."zip_code_geom")
  AND ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."end_station_longitude"  , t."end_station_latitude"  )), z."zip_code_geom")
GROUP BY t."usertype"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Pick the user type with the highest average temperature and show its averages.
SELECT *
FROM (
    SELECT t."usertype",
           AVG(w."temp") AS "avg_temp",
           AVG(w."prcp") AS "avg_prcp",
           AVG(w."wdsp") AS "avg_wdsp"
    FROM "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE"."CITIBIKE_TRIPS"  t
    JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."GEO_US_BOUNDARIES"."ZIP_CODES"       z
         ON z."zip_code" = '10019' AND z."state_code" = 'NY'
    JOIN "NEW_YORK_CITIBIKE_1"."NOAA_GSOD"."GSOD2018"                w
         ON w."stn" = '725033' AND w."wban" = '94728'
         AND w."year" = '2018'
         AND TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP(t."starttime"/1000000)) = TO_DATE(TO_DATE(w."year"||'-'||w."mo"||'-'||w."da'))
    WHERE ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."start_station_longitude", t."start_station_latitude")), z."zip_code_geom")
      AND ST_WITHIN(TO_GEOGRAPHY(POINT(t."end_station_longitude"  , t."end_station_latitude"  )), z."zip_code_geom")
    GROUP BY t."usertype"
)
ORDER BY "avg_temp" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
